From b2743744fd2d3abc43d86cb6dcc28e0941cbef10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: davmels <davmelous@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 07:21:03 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 56/61] llm_judge: structured verdicts, failure causes, zero
 weight for failed judge calls

structured: vLLM structured outputs, choice [Yes, No] for verdict (P(Yes) still read from the first
token's logprobs) and a JSON object {reasoning, verdict} with a length cap for justify. Judge calls are
counted by outcome (ok, no_verdict, http, timeout, other) apart from answers with nothing to judge,
with the first answers logged. mask_failures: a failed call marks its sample mask_sample in the
environment metadata; native rollouts now always carry mask_sample, GRPO's mask_sample filter drops
those samples from the loss, and the advantage estimator leaves them out of their group's baseline.

---
 nemo_rl/algorithms/grpo.py                    |  16 +++
 nemo_rl/environments/llm_judge_environment.py | 128 ++++++++++++++++--
 nemo_rl/experience/rollouts.py                |  11 ++
 3 files changed, 145 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

